# DotStack Specification: Axiom Tech V3 Technical Stack

## Status and compatibility

This is the V3 stack contract. It supersedes the V1 Streamlit/Pinecone-first description for new work while allowing legacy files to remain during migration. A production OCI deployment is not asserted by this document.

## Architecture shape

A Python modular monolith exposes a FastAPI boundary. The backend keeps API, application use cases, LangGraph orchestration, ingestion, retrieval adapters, and model gateways independently testable without splitting them into networked services. The React/Vite client consumes the versioned HTTP API.

## Primary components

| Concern | V3 choice | Rationale |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Runtime | Python 3.11+ | Mature document, AI, and API ecosystem. |
| API | FastAPI plus Uvicorn | Typed HTTP contract, health probes, and clear client boundary. |
| Orchestration | LangGraph StateGraph | Real conditional workflow with routing, evidence grading, bounded rewrites, synthesis, and fallback. |
| Default vector store | Persistent ChromaDB | Local-first, secret-free retrieval that can persist on an OCI volume. |
| Optional vector store | Pinecone adapter boundary | Intentionally fails transparently until a deployment-specific adapter is completed. |
| Default model behavior | Deterministic local providers | Repeatable offline development and tests. |
| Optional model provider | NVIDIA NIM | Opt-in remote inference; credentials are never required for local functionality. |
| Ingestion | Python extractors and normalized metadata | Multi-format corpus ingestion with source/file/chunk/locator preservation. |
| Web client | React + Vite | Accessible, independently deployable browser workspace. |
| Delivery | Docker, Docker Compose, OCI-compatible images | Repeatable local topology and a clear OCI handoff. |

## V3 runtime modes

| Mode | Vector store | Model behavior | Required secrets |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Offline/local default | ChromaDB at AXIOM_CHROMA_PATH | Deterministic providers | None |
| Optional NVIDIA mode | ChromaDB by default | NVIDIA NIM when AXIOM_NVIDIA_ENABLED=true | Relevant NVIDIA key(s) |
| Optional Pinecone mode | Pinecone adapter boundary | Deterministic or NVIDIA | Requires a completed deployment adapter; otherwise fails transparently |

A selected optional provider must fail transparently if it is incomplete or unavailable; it must not masquerade as the local default.

## Configuration

- AXIOM_DOCUMENTS_DIR identifies the internal corpus.
- AXIOM_VECTOR_BACKEND defaults to chroma.
- AXIOM_CHROMA_PATH and AXIOM_CHROMA_COLLECTION configure persistent local retrieval.
- AXIOM_NVIDIA_ENABLED defaults to false.
- AXIOM_CORS_ORIGINS controls browser origins at the FastAPI boundary.
- PINECONE_* and model keys are optional runtime secrets, never committed values.

See .env.example for safe defaults and docs/deployment.md for container/OCI guidance.

## Delivery constraints

- Mount durable storage for ChromaDB in any container runtime expected to retain an index.
- Keep API and frontend images separable; the frontend reverse-proxies /api/ in the local Compose topology.
- Preserve source metadata across ingestion and retrieval.
- Do not add a cloud provider, external vector database, or external LLM as a mandatory development dependency.
- Do not treat a legacy UI, a static build artifact, or a simulated response as evidence of V3 API behavior.
